{
  "$comment": "Bharat's Claude Code setup. MERGE this into your user-global ~/.claude/settings.json so it applies in every directory. extraKnownMarketplaces makes marketplaces installable; enabledPlugins turns them on everywhere. ecc, probity (TDD/rule enforcement), memsearch (semantic session memory), openai-codex (cross-model reviews), and the non-default trailofbits plugins are registered but intentionally NOT enabled — one '/plugin install' away (see README cheatsheet). agent-teams@claude-code-workflows is explicitly disabled: it still calls the TeamCreate/TeamDelete tools removed in Claude Code v2.1.178 (Jun 2026). superpowers and mattpocock-skills are consumed from claude-plugins-official (SHA-pinned by Anthropic) since 2026-09-22; their old marketplace keys are set to false, and bootstrap.sh forces a repo-side false onto existing machines so the duplicates are disabled. External marketplaces are SHA-pinned (source.sha, recorded 2026-09-22; bootstrap's own marketplace is left unpinned so consumers track this repo). scripts/check_upstream.py reports pin drift; bump a sha only after re-vetting (docs/supply-chain.md). permissions: defaultMode auto (classifier reviews, no per-tool prompts) is applied only where the user has no defaultMode; allow pre-approves routine dev commands and the fetch/search/agent tools so they never prompt in Manual mode and skip the classifier in auto mode; deny blocks credential reads and destructive git/rm forms in every mode. bootstrap merges all three (allow/deny as unions, defaultMode only if absent).",
